"python.analysis.packageIndexDepths": [
    {
      "name": "langgraph",
      "depth": 4
    },
    {
      "name": "langchain",
      "depth": 3
    },
    { "name": "langchain_community", "depth": 3 }
    ]
```
    
The above entry needs to be added to vscode `settings.json` file for auto imports to find the packages. The issue is at depth level 2 for eg. `from langgraph.types ` here `langgraph` is depth level 1 and `types.py` is at depth 2. Without a `__init__.py` or `__init__.pyi` file, any `.py` files i.e modules at depth level 2 are not being indexed for auto imports even if the max depth is greater than 2 (As you can see I have langgraph depth set at 4). 
 
 So if anyone wants to have auto import support for langgraph or langchain they need to first add the above configuration in their vscode `settings.json` (one time setup) and then add an `__init__.pyi` file into the package inside the `.venv` (cumbersome setup/hack). This is not ideal since if we upgrade the langgraph package again one needs to add this `__init__.pyi`. If the PR is approved then the cumbersome part of this setup is avoided.

