@hinthornw — This PR adds the `ERROR`/`INTERRUPT` cache guard to `SyncPregelLoop.put_writes` that was already present in `AsyncPregelLoop.put_writes`. Without it, failed or interrupted tasks get cached in sync mode and are replayed on subsequent runs instead of being re-executed.

The fix is a 3-line addition mirroring the async path. A regression test (`test_sync_cache_does_not_store_error_writes`) has also been added — it fails without the fix and passes with it.

